If the nethack binary was compiled with both tty and X11, then
putting "OPTIONS=windowtype:tty" in your ~/.nethackrc should start
nethack using the tty window port.  If not... either get another
rpm, or compile your own nethack.

In a linux X terminal (without a vga font), IBMgraphics doesn't work,
and DECgraphics mostly works, although some symbols look weird. For
best results, turn both IBMgraphics and DECgraphics off.
OPTIONS=!IBMgraphics,!DECgraphics

If you want to have it _exactly_ like your DOS version, you can
start your terminal program with a vga-font.  At least one vga-font
(vga.pcf) comes with xdosemu.

